# A reply arrived on a watched thread while the session was closed. Opening the
# session the ordinary way, from the list, should hand it the reply rather than
# leave it behind the inbox badge. Closing the session and opening it again must not
# deliver the same reply a second time.

size 110x30
arg --mux
session existing-app Existing app session
held_reply https://github.com/o/r/issues/12

wait_for Existing app session
dump 01-list-with-held-reply

press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling
wait_for Fake Copilot received: A new comment arrived on https://github.com/o/r/issues/12
dump 02-reopened-and-woken

# CST keeps a delivered pointer on file until it sees the composer emptied, which
# real Copilot reports through a hook as the turn starts. The stub has no hooks, so
# an Enter typed into the pane stands in for it. Without one, closing the session
# is closing it with the pointer unread, and CST rightly delivers it again.
press enter
wait 1500

# Ends the session, not just leaves it: the next Enter has to start it again.
press ctrl+b x
wait_gone Fake Copilot is idling
expect Existing app session
dump 03-closed-back-at-list

press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling
wait 3000
expect_not Fake Copilot received
dump 04-reopened-again
